          "comment": "#993 belt (the FIX 3 precedent): this dropoff-phase surface can win a frame that STILL carries DoorDash's nav arrival banner — `dropoff_navigation`'s own reject (Continue / Complete Delivery / Mark as delivered / complete_delivery_steps_button) hands the arrival-MOMENT frame to whichever arrived-phase rule matches, and nav_arriving rejects bottom-sheet frames, so neither of the two rules that already masked `arriving_at_title` covers it. The node is id-BEARING, so the id-less name/address entries elsewhere in this block structurally cannot reach it (`hasNoId` conjunct). Whole token, no normalize — it is a customer ADDRESS on every dropoff-phase surface (see dropoff_navigation for the full reasoning). Inert on any frame without the node; `DropoffBannerRedactParityTest` pins that EVERY rule in this file carries it, so a new dropoff surface cannot forget.",
