          "plainMask": true
        },
        {
          "comment": "#1039 belt: the LABEL-anchored half of the subpremise mask — an `Apt/Suite` label node followed by its value, whatever spelling that value carries (`Unit 4202` shipped raw 2026-08-14). Both label spellings are enumerated because `hasPrecedingSiblingText` is an exact, un-trimmed equality; whole-node `plainMask` because a unit number is a bounded ~10^4 alphabet. Ordered ahead of every generic shape entry in this block: `maskNode` is first-match-wins, and a digit-leading value (`101 B`) would otherwise be claimed and HASHED by the id-less street shape. See `dropoff_handoff` for the full reasoning. Inert without the label; pinned by the #1039 parity test.",
